{
  "requirement": "When source-access policy denies a path that a model tool call names\nexplicitly, the harness MUST return a tool error naming the path and the reason\nit cannot be read, add no evidence input, and continue the assessment.\nDiscovery and search MUST leave denied candidates out of their entries,\nreporting untracked ones under {cite}`requirements.authoring.not_listed`. Malformed tool\narguments and ordinary read failures MUST also return explanatory tool errors.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged the tests adequate for `requirements.authoring.read_denial`. I did not request any implementation source, because the supplied tests were enough to map each obligation to scenarios and assertions.\n\n**1. A denied explicit path returns a tool error naming the path and the reason, adds no evidence input, and the assessment continues.**\n- `src/authoring/tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[generated_evidence_is_excluded_from_reads_search_and_discovery]`\n  - It requests `evidence/old.json`, including the `./` form, through `habeas`, `list_files`, `ripgrep` and `ast_grep`, and through symlink aliases.\n  - It asserts `PermissionDenied`, that the message contains the path and \"generated evidence\", and that `recorded_inputs` is empty.\n- `fn[cargo_output_is_discovered_and_read_without_building_or_allowing_other_target_files]` denies a path by a `disallow` rule across all four tools. It asserts that the message names the path and says \"disallowed\".\n- `fn[outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs]` covers a disallowed file through `outline`.\n- `fn[untracked_diagnostics_name_git_add_and_an_allow_rule]` checks the untracked reason. The message names the path, `git add` and a `habeas.toml allow rule`, and the harness stages nothing.\n- `fn[requests_through_symlinks_leaving_the_project_are_denials]` covers symlink escapes. It asserts `PermissionDenied` and \"outside the project\" for every tool.\n- The policy unit tests in `src/authoring/access.rs` cover allow/disallow precedence, alias targets and disallowed ancestors. They assert `PermissionDenied` and that the message contains the path. This includes `fn[disallowed_ancestors_cannot_redirect_reads_into_allowed_targets]`.\n- Continuation is checked end to end in three tests:\n  - `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[a_read_through_a_symlink_leaving_the_project_returns_an_error_to_the_model]` checks that the model's second request carries the path and reason, that no file content is leaked, and that the evidence omits the file.\n  - `tests/authoring_batch.rs#fn[a_denied_read_returns_an_error_and_its_assessment_continues]` checks two requests, `tool_failures` of 1, a completed outcome, and that the denied file is not recorded.\n  - `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[explicit_untracked_reads_return_an_untracked_error_and_the_assessment_continues]` covers all four tools. It checks the second request, the absence of the hidden content, a completed outcome and no recorded input.\n\n**2. Discovery and search leave denied candidates out of their entries and report untracked ones under `not_listed`.**\n- `fn[allowed_ignored_and_external_sources_are_discoverable_but_disallowed_descendants_are_not]` asserts exact listings and search results. The disallowed `generated/private` descendants are absent from the listing, the ripgrep matches and the ast-grep matches.\n- `fn[cargo_output_is_discovered_and_read_without_building_or_allowing_other_target_files]` shows that a disallowed path vanishes from the listing, the ripgrep results and the ast-grep results.\n- `fn[listings_and_searches_name_untracked_files_without_their_contents]` checks `not_listed` for `list_files`, `ripgrep` and `ast_grep`.\n  - Each entry has the reason `untracked`.\n  - No content is leaked and `inputs` is empty.\n  - The disallowed `secret.rs` and the generated `evidence/note.txt` do not appear in `not_listed`.\n  - `not_listed` is omitted when nothing untracked matches.\n  - The path spellings `./src`, `src/../src` and an absolute path give the same result.\n- `fn[git_tools_allow_staged_and_dirty_sources_but_hide_untracked_files]` and `fn[git_symlink_reads_require_both_the_alias_and_target_to_be_tracked]` check that untracked files are hidden from entries.\n- The `not_listed` details (paging, ordering) belong to `requirements.authoring.not_listed`, which the subject only cites.\n\n**3. Malformed tool arguments and ordinary read failures return explanatory tool errors.**\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#fn[malformed_and_failed_reads_return_to_the_model_and_the_assessment_continues]` runs six cases through the full `assess` loop: bad types, a missing field, conflicting forms, a missing file, an absent item and a line out of range. It asserts that each error is not `PermissionDenied`, that it reaches the model in the second request, that the assessment continues, and that no input is recorded.\n- `fn[operating_system_permission_failures_are_ordinary_read_failures]` covers OS permission failures. They are ordinary failures, not denials.\n- `fn[failed_listings_return_explanatory_tool_errors]`, `fn[search_records_nothing_clamps_at_eof_and_reports_failures]` and `fn[ast_grep_returns_innermost_nodes_of_the_language_and_reports_failures]` cover malformed arguments, invalid patterns and rules, and syntax errors.\n- `fn[requests_for_book_or_target_output_are_ordinary_read_failures]` covers build-output requests. `fn[unpermitted_requests_outside_the_project_are_recoverable_tool_errors]` covers requests outside the project.\n- `fn[paged_inputs_carry_their_definitions_and_deliver_only_their_own_inputs]` covers `next_page` token errors. `fn[additional_read_flow_searches_outlines_and_reads_a_rust_file]` covers `github` argument and read errors.\n\n**Delegated obligations.** The mandatory-input abort, untracked and build-output specifics are refinements. I checked only that their tests carry the right markers, and I did not reassess their adequacy.\n\nEvery obligation, both failure classes and every tool (`habeas`, `outline`, `list_files`, `ripgrep`, `ast_grep`) has a test with a real assertion. I found no unacknowledged gap.",
  "references": "6ad9d05b356cfbef0240f25ffca37400d333581fc3b44a94dad325f115437753",
